From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: program the MTU field for runtime WAN1

The direct WAN1 role added by patch 933 intentionally retains the logical
LAN role. Consequently the legacy !airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev() test skips the
FE WAN MTU register for that device even though the caller updates PPE MTU.

Program WAN_MTU1_MASK when the device owns WAN1. Preserve the existing WAN0
condition and the VLAN_ETH_HLEN adjustment from the pinned PonWrt stack.
WAN0 and WAN1 occupy independent fields in REG_WAN_MTU0; a separate WAN1
register must not be invented. The read-modify-write preserves WAN0.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2114,7 +2114,11 @@ static void airoha_dev_set_mtu(struct net_device *netdev)
 
 	airoha_ppe_set_mtu(dev);
-	if (!airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev))
+	if (dev->hw_wan_slot == AIROHA_HW_WAN1)
+		airoha_fe_rmw(dev->eth, REG_WAN_MTU0,
+			      WAN_MTU1_MASK,
+			      FIELD_PREP(WAN_MTU1_MASK, netdev->mtu + VLAN_ETH_HLEN));
+	else if (!airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev))
 		airoha_fe_rmw(dev->eth, REG_WAN_MTU0,
 			      WAN_MTU0_MASK,
 			      FIELD_PREP(WAN_MTU0_MASK, netdev->mtu + VLAN_ETH_HLEN));
 }
